  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LBH&apos;s Legal Aid work linked to Civil, Political, Economic, Social and Cultural Rights.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LBH is a foundation providing free legal aid to people on a range of topics covering all economic, social, civil and political rights. They have been active in working with land rights issues since the Tsunami, in addition to their regular work.
This two year project focuses especially on laws linked to the planned formation of a Truth and Reconciliation Commission for Aceh, as set out in the MoU, and the eradication of laws which impede on freedom of expression. Further, they will continue to raise awareness amongst the grass roots population of their rights, especially linked to post-Tsunami rehabilitation and post-conflict issues, and will try to help ensure policy makers take people&apos;s rights into consideration when developing new local laws. These focus areas are in addition to their on-going work of providing free legal aid to the general population on a wide range of issues.</narrative>
  </description>
